[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-PLAN-WP-20
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Reject executable constructs that lowering would silently omit
STATEMENT: >>>
Unsupported executable constructs fail explicitly; supported assertions and final blocks have demonstrable effects. A positive parser/exporter exit alone never satisfies acceptance.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Inferred planning acceptance for WP-20, P0, relative scope M. UHDM executable construct auditing is active in native/uhdm/rtl_audit.h (RtlExecutableAudit called from native/uhdm/rtl.cpp before flattening), rejecting concurrent/immediate assertions, assume/cover, final blocks, clocking blocks, programs, interfaces and primitive instances/arrays with source coordinates; immediate runtime assert IR is implemented under VS-RTL-ASSERT-001. Full coverage across additional UHDM constructs (covergroups, classes, force/release, specify blocks, UDPs) and final-block execution remain tracked. Dependencies: WP-01. Product IDs: VS-QUAL-001, VS-RTL-ASSERT-001. GitHub issue: https://github.com/jeffadickson/VeloSim/issues/21. Library evaluation: LIB-01, LIB-06.
<<<
